## **6. Register the staff routes**

Add these routes inside your existing authenticated router. Keep your existing `RequireAuth` component and adapt the user/permission mapping to your actual authentication response.

```

import { Route } from "react-router-dom";
import StaffLayout from "./portals/staff/StaffLayout";
import StaffDashboardRouter from "./portals/staff/StaffDashboardRouter";

// Example only: use your existing authenticated user and logout handler.
<Route
  path="/staff"
  element={
    <RequireAuth allowedRoles={["ADMIN", "PRINCIPAL", "REGISTRAR",
      "FINANCE_OFFICER", "HR", "LECTURER", "LIBRARIAN",
      "IT_SUPPORT", "HOD", "ADMISSIONS_OFFICER",
      "EXAMINATIONS_OFFICER", "QUALITY_ASSURANCE",
      "STUDENT_AFFAIRS", "HOSTEL_OFFICER", "ICT_TECHNICIAN",
      "PROCUREMENT_OFFICER", "STORES_OFFICER",
      "COMMUNICATIONS_OFFICER", "RECEPTIONIST",
      "SECURITY_OFFICER", "TRANSPORT_OFFICER"]}
    >
      <StaffLayout
        user={authenticatedStaffUser}
        onLogout={handleLogout}
      />
    </RequireAuth>
  }
>
  <Route path="dashboard" element={<StaffDashboardRouter />} />
</Route>

```

`RequireAuth`, `authenticatedStaffUser` and `handleLogout` above represent your existing application authentication implementation; they are not new functions supplied by these files.

